  <section class="chapter">

    <h2>Prologue</h2>

    <p>Before the Beginning</p>

  </section>

  <article class="story">

    <p class="first-letter">
      Before there were kingdoms, before there were temples,
      before the first written word was pressed into clay,
      there was a memory.
    </p>

    <p>
      It existed before the names of nations, before the borders
      of kingdoms, and before humanity had learned to measure
      the passage of time.
    </p>

    <p>
      The oldest people remembered it differently.
      Some spoke of a light that descended from the heavens.
      Others spoke of a voice that came from the deep places
      beneath the earth.
    </p>

    <p>
      Priests carved fragments of the story into stone.
      Scribes copied what they believed they understood.
      Generations passed, and the original meaning slowly
      disappeared beneath layers of interpretation.
    </p>

    <p>
      But the memory itself never died.
    </p>

    <p>
      It waited.
    </p>

    <p>
      And somewhere beneath the ruins of the ancient world,
      something had been left behind.
    </p>

    <p>
      Something that was never meant to be found.
    </p>

    <p>
      Until now.
    </p>

  </article>

